{title: Blessed Be Your Glorious Name}
{subtitle: Nehemiah 9:5; 10:11; 10:28–30; 11:22}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [F] |
| [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]The Levites stood in the [Bb]court that day
[F]Jeshua and Kadmiel led the [C]way
[Dm]Bani and Hashabneiah [Bb]stood tall
Sherebi[F]ah and Hodiah heard the [C]call
[Bb]Shebaniah and Pethahiah joined [Dm]in
To bless [C]the Lord from past to p[A]resent
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Dm]Blessed be your glorious [Bb]name
Which is ex[F]alted above all [C]fame
Above every [Dm]blessing and [Bb]praise
We lift our [F]voices [C]in the [Dm]haze
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
They bound themselves with a [Bb]curse and an oath
To [F]walk in the Law of [C]God
[Dm]Given through Moses [Bb]the servant true
To keep [F]and carry out all that is [C]due
With [Bb]judgments and statutes of the [Dm]Lord
Bound to the [C]covenant, a solid [A]word
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Dm]Blessed be your glorious [Bb]name
Which is ex[F]alted above all [C]fame
Above every [Dm]blessing and [Bb]praise
We lift our [F]voices in [C]the [Dm]haze
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
In Je[Bb]rusalem the work continued
[Dm]Levites served as it was intended
[F]Uzzi son of Bani served there
[C]Descendants of Asaph in the [Bb]prayer
[Dm]Singers in the [C]house of [Bb]God
Keeping the faith [C]of the old [A]road
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Dm]Blessed be your glorious [Bb]name
Which is ex[F]alted above all [C]fame
Above every [Dm]blessing and [Bb]praise
We lift our [F]voices [C]in the haze
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Dm]Blessed be your glorious [Bb]name
Ex[F]alted above every [C][Dm]fame
{end_of_verse}
